TI  - Intergenerational views of hardiness in critical care nurses.
PG  - 214-20
LID - 10.1097/DCC.0b013e3181ac4b82 [doi]
AB  - As all nurses are aware, healthcare is experiencing a time of great change. This
      change can lead to stress, nurse vacancy rates, and burnout. However, the effects
      of stress can be mitigated by personal hardiness. This article presents an
      overview of hardiness, as well as the results of a qualitative study to describe
      hardiness in the workplace.
